# DPU Attendance — project defaults

Face check-in & HR attendance system: InsightFace `buffalo_l` (512-d) + pgvector, or Face Core BFF (`FACE_CORE_ENABLED`). Docker stack behind nginx.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `API-Fast/` | FastAPI + InsightFace + GPU queue + Hybrid Check-In/Out + Shift Late/OT + Excel/CSV Export |
| `Web-Manage/` | Angular 19 admin (kiosk at `/company/timestamp-face`; shared list UI under `src/app/shared/`) |
| `docker/` | nginx gateway + DB init |
| `docs/` | SETUP, ARCHITECTURE, API, RUNBOOK, BACKLOG, agent guide (`CURSOR-AGENT.md`) |
| `API-Fast/src/security/` | JWT, authz middleware, tenancy deps (`assert_company_access`, `assert_member_company_access`, `assert_encoding_company_access`), passwords/lockout |
| `API-Fast/src/services/` | audit, multi-replica notification outbox (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`), storage retention, observability, face match |
| `.cursor/rules/` | Always-on + scoped agent rules |
| `.cursor/skills/` | Task workflows (`dpu-face-kiosk`, `dpu-docker-rebuild`, `dpu-web-manage-ui`) |

## Runtime

```bash
# Shared local Postgres (sibling ../dev-postgres on dev-net, schema dpu) — preferred for local
docker network create dev-net   # once
# cd ../dev-postgres && docker compose up -d
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.gpu.yml \
  -f docker-compose.external-db.yml up -d --build

# Builtin dpu-db (legacy local volume) — omit external-db.yml
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.gpu.yml up -d --build

# Same-host BFF: Face Core on face-net (prefer dual-API for single-host saturation).
docker network create face-net
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.prod.yml -f docker-compose.face-core.yml up -d --build

# Local DPU → remote Face Core (dev / A+1): FACE_CORE_URL=http://<host>:8081
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.face-core-remote.yml up -d --build
```

- Admin: `http://localhost/`
- API docs: `http://localhost/docs`
- Kiosk: `http://localhost/company/timestamp-face`
- Loadtest: `scripts/kiosk-load/` · monolith saturation `docs/KIOSK-LOADTEST-SATURATION.md` · Face Core identify `docs/FACE-CORE-IDENTIFY-CAPACITY.md`

Code is **baked into images** — rebuild after source changes (`api`, `api-gpu1`, `admin`, `nginx` as needed).

## Security & Performance Baseline (Phase 1 & Phase 2)

- `SECRET_KEY` ≥ 32 chars from env; API refuses the placeholder when `AUTH_FAIL_FAST=true`
- Every route except `/auth/login`, `/auth/refresh*`, `/health`, `/ready`, `/metrics`, `/` requires a Bearer JWT (`src/security/middleware.py` `AuthzMiddleware`)
- `companyId`, `memberId`, and `faceEncodingId` in paths/forms/bodies must be bound to the caller via `assert_request_company_access`, `assert_member_company_access`, or `assert_encoding_company_access` in `src/security/deps.py`
- Both `/auth/login` and `/auth/refresh` enforce `assert_not_locked` and verify active status (`StatusType.ENABLE`)
- 1:N face matching (`search_face_pgvector`) and check-in finalization filter active employees only (`CompanyEmployee.deletedAt IS NULL`, `Member.deletedAt IS NULL`, `Member.status == ENABLE`)
- Kiosk WebSocket `session` carries `token`, continuously enforces `token_exp`, and caps per-connection in-flight tasks via `asyncio.Semaphore(4)`
- Hybrid Check-In / Check-Out (`AUTO` / `CHECK_IN` / `CHECK_OUT`), per-company work shifts (`shift:{companyId}`), and `.xlsx`/`.csv` exports are aligned to `Asia/Bangkok` timezone
- Writes are audited asynchronously (`asyncio.create_task(_audit(...))`); notifications go through `notification_outbox` with `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and `asyncio.to_thread`

## Agent defaults

- Prefer existing patterns; do not invent a second face stack
- Check-in UX is the **admin kiosk** (`/company/timestamp-face`); there is no separate mobile app
- Do not commit unless asked; do not put secrets in rules/docs
- After API/UI/nginx changes: rebuild and verify `/health`, `/ready`, queue-stats (with a token)
- Local `.env` must have a real `SECRET_KEY` before `docker compose up`, or `api` exits at import
- Thai UI copy is OK for kiosk; keep code/comments in English unless the file already uses Thai
